{
  "name": "SystemArchitecture",
  "internal_name": "SystemArchitecture",
  "focus": "High-level USSD system boundary and end-to-end flows: users call the upgradeable USSD token for collateral-backed minting and accounting; control-role administrators configure collateral, oracles, and the swap router; the authorized rebalancer reads pool and collateral data, calls USSD mint/burn/swap interfaces, and interacts with Uniswap; oracle implementations source prices from Chainlink feeds or Uniswap V3 TWAP pools. Show contracts, interfaces, external protocols and tokens, authorization boundaries, and the direction of calls and data.",
